    "current_example": {
      "math_academy_id": "e-9399",
      "problem": "Calculate the value of $\\dfrac{1}{3} - \\dfrac{5}{6}.$",
      "worked_solution": "We write $\\dfrac{1}{3}$ as $\\dfrac{2}{6}$ and then we simply subtract the numerators. This gives\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{2}{6} - \\dfrac{5}{6} = \\dfrac{2 - 5}{6}.\n$$\n\nNow, we work out $2 - 5$ using a number line:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14148354/assets/c63a3db44b79e751c7cf1a49dcebcbb1d00cea0427da4ef271d07646e4be2748.png)\n\nSo we get\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{2 - 5}{6} = \\dfrac{-3}{6} = -\\dfrac{3}{6}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we simplify:\n\n$$\n-\\dfrac{3}{6} = -\\dfrac{3 \\div 3}{6 \\div 3} =-\\dfrac{1}{2}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{3} - \\dfrac{5}{6} = -\\dfrac{1}{2}.\n$$",
